<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xri version="1.0">
   <description>
      <p>astro-pi — unified PixInsight distribution (scarter4work)</p>
      <p>NukeX integration/stretching module + EZ Stretch BSC script suite.</p>
      <p>Repository: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/scarter4work/astro-pi/main/repository/</p>
   </description>
   <platform os="linux" arch="x64" version="1.8.0:2.0.0">
      <package fileName="20261013-linux-x64-NukeX-5.2.0.1.tar.gz" sha1="07f040784c93acf931c76439f640e59b12f22830" type="module" releaseDate="20261013">
         <title>NukeX</title>
         <description>
            <p>
               <b>NukeX 5.1.0.3</b>
            </p>
            <p>v5.1.0.3: now loads on any Linux that runs PixInsight 1.9.5 (glibc 2.34 or newer: Ubuntu 22.04+, Debian 12+, Rocky/RHEL 9+, current Fedora/Arch). Earlier builds only loaded on very new distributions and needed the Ceres, glog, gflags and OpenMP libraries installed. It no longer depends on any of them; the OpenCL loader is built in, and GPU drivers are found exactly as before. Also fixes dual-narrowband (HaO3 / S2O3, e.g. Askar ColorMagic D1/D2) stacks failing with &quot;Camera not in QE DB&quot;: real camera names such as &quot;ZWO ASI585MC Air&quot; now resolve, and the HaO3/S2O3 filter classes are in the database.</p>
            <p>v5.1.0.2: Phase B batch sizing is now bounded by available system RAM (not just GPU VRAM), fixing an out-of-memory kill on hosts where RAM is smaller than VRAM headroom (e.g. a 16 GB GPU on a 30 GB machine). Per-batch host footprint is now shown in the Phase B log.</p>
            <p>Astrophotography integration and stretching module. v5.1.0 is a color-science overhaul: physically-grounded, QE-database-driven channel decomposition for OSC/mono and dual-narrowband workflows (fixes the v4 green cast), with per-channel frame accounting for heterogeneous-geometry batches. The QE database is compiled into the module, so it installs with no extra files.</p>
            <p>v5.1.0.1: broadband / clear filter-wheel slot labels (Full, Clear, None, Open, L-Pro, L-QEF, UV/IR-cut) on Bayer frames now route as plain OSC instead of hard-aborting the stack; corrected stale &quot;v4&quot; labels in the UI to v5.</p>
         </description>
      </package>
      <package fileName="20261013-linux-x64-PICopilot-0.2.2.0.tar.gz" sha1="c1edbd214718e2d6d0a52830b1cd2ce8eab20f5b" type="module" releaseDate="20261013">
         <title>PI Copilot</title>
         <description>
            <p>
               <b>PI Copilot</b>
            </p>
            <p>PI Copilot — AI assistant panel for PixInsight (bring your own Anthropic API key).</p>
            <p>v0.2.1.1: now loads on any Linux that runs PixInsight 1.9.5 (glibc 2.34 or newer: Ubuntu 22.04+, Debian 12+, Rocky/RHEL 9+). Earlier builds only loaded on very new distributions.</p>
         </description>
      </package>
      <package fileName="20261013-linux-x64-GaiaDepthGradeSidecar-1.0.8.tar.gz" sha1="9bb92ab3b6c336ccd7158ab3c2eb77df8ca697cf" type="generic" releaseDate="20261013">
         <title>Gaia Depth Grade sidecar</title>
         <description>
            <p>
               <b>Gaia Depth Grade sidecar 1.0.8</b>
            </p>
            <p>The image-processing program used by the Gaia Depth Grade script (install both). It is installed as bin/gaia-depth-grade-sidecar and its licences in doc/scripts/GaiaDepthGrade/. It is a self-contained program (Python with NumPy, SciPy, Astropy, photutils, astroquery and Pillow); no Python installation is needed.</p>
            <p>1.0.8: now delivered by PixInsight&apos;s update system instead of being downloaded by the script; 61 MB instead of 100 MB; runs on any Linux that runs PixInsight (glibc 2.34 or newer: Ubuntu 22.04+, Debian 12+, Rocky/RHEL 9+) — 1.0.7 only started on very new distributions. Image results are identical to 1.0.7.</p>
         </description>
      </package>
   </platform>
   <platform os="all" arch="noarch" version="1.8.0:2.0.0">
      <package fileName="EZStretch_v1.0.11.zip" sha1="2e9b1ae6f14fb3b0980f78caca35741facdf1779" type="script" releaseDate="20261013">
