      <package fileName="gaia-depth-grade_v1.0.13.zip" sha1="7f736f18fa3d02511e2fd10941f567a497dfd0d2" type="script" releaseDate="20261013">
         <title>Gaia Depth Grade</title>
         <description>
            <p>
               <b>Gaia Depth Grade v1.0.13</b>
            </p>
            <p>Physically-grounded depth grade for astrophotographs using Gaia distances. Defaults to the offline local Gaia DR3 database (the one PixInsight uses for plate-solving; no network use); an online option queries the ESA Gaia archive over HTTPS for Bailer-Jones distances. Linux x64 only: needs the &quot;Gaia Depth Grade sidecar&quot; package from this repository, and StarXTerminator. Documentation, including network use, the programs it runs and the files it writes: doc/scripts/GaiaDepthGrade/GaiaDepthGrade.html.</p>
            <p>v1.0.13 (sidecar 1.0.8): the sidecar program now comes from PixInsight&apos;s update system (package &quot;Gaia Depth Grade sidecar&quot;); the script no longer downloads, unpacks or installs anything, and no longer uses ~/.astro-pi (you may delete ~/.astro-pi/gaia-depth-grade). All working files and online Gaia query results now live in a private per-user directory, ~/.cache/gaia-depth-grade (mode 0700, checked before use), instead of the shared /tmp/gaia_depth_grade and PixInsight&apos;s bin directory. Ships its documentation. Image results are unchanged.</p>
            <p>v1.0.12 (sidecar 1.0.7): enlarged (near) stars now wear a realistic STAR-SHINE HALO. The halo&apos;s radial shape is stacked from the frame&apos;s own bright, unsaturated, isolated stars and tinted to each star&apos;s own colour, with amplitude anchored to its real peak brightness — replacing the achromatic Gaussian blob that read as fake. Frames with too few clean reference stars fall back to a Moffat profile (with a warning).</p>
            <p>v1.0.11 (sidecar 1.0.6): adds optional NEBULA DEPTH. A new checkbox grades the starless layer too — dark dust/globules come forward, the diffuse glow recedes, with gentle atmospheric perspective and noise-cored structural relief. The spatial variation comes from the nebula&apos;s own structure; the overall strength is calibrated by the Gaia matched-star distance spread, so the nebula depth matches the stars. Opt-in (off by default) with live Nebula depth / atmospheric / structure sliders.</p>
         </description>
      </package>
   </platform>
</xri>
